WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 7 Student Video
Unit 2, Lesson 3: Pantheism

1
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.630
Star Wars is one of the most successful film series in history.

2
00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:23.850
As a kid, I remember the epic battles between Luke Skywalker and Darth Vader.

3
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:28.790
In fact, today, I still enjoy bringing my own kids to the most recent Star Wars

4
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:33.770
film. The cinematography, the special effects, and the storyline have captured

5
00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:34.530
generations.

6
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.290
Star Wars also introduced the West to the worldview known as pantheism.

7
00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.050
As

8
00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.340
we have seen, naturalism is the worldview that says only physical things exist and

9
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.320
there are no supernatural forces.

10
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:57.280
By contrast, pantheism is the worldview that says all is divine and there's no

11
00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.040
distinction between creator and creation.

12
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.880
Like naturalism, pantheism offers answers to our four big worldview questions.

13
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.340
The first question is, what is real?

14
00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:12.160
Well, on pantheism, all is divine.

15
00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.320
God is not a personal being whom we know, but is inseparable from the universe.

16
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.600
God is more like a cosmic energy that pervades all things.

17
00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.620
Sound familiar? This is like the force in Star Wars.

18
00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:31.820
In essence, all is one. Our second question is, what is man?

19
00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:38.140
Well, if God is one with the universe and all is divine, then by necessity, man

20
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:43.980
is divine. Man is God. Pantheists will sometimes refer to human beings

21
00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:49.640
as gods or goddesses in embryo. So rather than seeing human beings as

22
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:55.620
uniquely created in the image of God but broken by sin, pantheists see human beings

23
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.340
as essentially good and divine.

24
00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:04.420
Our third worldview question is, what happens at death?

25
00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:10.320
The goal of mankind on pantheism is to achieve enlightenment and to escape the

26
00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.340
cycle of reincarnation. And this is accomplished

27
00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.400
through practices

28
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.200
such as channeling, meditation, and yoga.

29
00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:23.320
And then, like a drop falling into a river, we achieve enlightenment and become

30
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.460
absorbed into the oneness of the universe.

31
00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:37.400
The fourth worldview question is, what is the basis for right and wrong?

32
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:43.060
Since on pantheism, all is one, distinctions are ultimately artificial.

33
00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:48.960
There is no distinction between Creator and creation, between God and man, between

34
00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.160
right and wrong. Morality is an illusion.

35
00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:58.360
Since good and evil don't exist, ultimately morality is

36
00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:58.700
relative.

37
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.820
Like naturalism, pantheism is nothing new.

38
00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.600
Some of the ideas we see in the Star Wars films have their roots in ancient Eastern

39
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:12.560
religions such as Hinduism and Buddhism.

40
00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:18.420
In fact, Paul likely addressed some pantheists in his speech at Mars Hill

41
00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.980
as recorded in Acts chapter 17.

42
00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.980
Pantheism is not new, but it is in direct conflict and contrast with a Christian

43
00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:33.340
worldview. The biggest question is, can it adequately capture reality as we know it

44
00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.720
and experience it?

